[505.764459, "o", "[10/23/26 10:10:48] INFO     all.holmesgpt.driver - HolmesGPT answer:                                                                       \r\n                             **ROOT CAUSE**                                                                                                 \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             - **Faulty component:** `Pod reservation-57b8ccd5dc-48mqt` (part of the *reservation* deployment)              \r\n                             - **What failed:** The container exited with `exitCode 2` and the log line `panic: no reachable servers` while \r\n                             trying to open a MongoDB connection (`mongodb-reservation:27017`).                                             \r\n                             - **Why it broke:** The MongoDB pod `mongodb-reservation-5994859869-nsg4b` was not yet running when the        \r\n                             reservation pod started. Its `startTime` is `2026‑10‑23T10:06:25Z`, while the reservation pod attempted the DB \r\n                             connection at `2026‑10‑23T10:06:21Z`. The DNS name resolved, but the service had no ready endpoints, causing   \r\n                             the driver to report “no reachable servers”. The reservation container crashed, was restarted (restartCount =  \r\n                             2), and succeeded only after the DB became ready.                                                              \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **Evidence**                                                                                                   \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             | Resource | Observation |                                                                                     \r\n                             |----------|-------------|                                                                                     \r\n                             | `reservation-57b8ccd5dc-48mqt` – container status | `lastState.terminated.exitCode=2`, `reason=Error`,       \r\n                             `restartCount=2` |                                                                                             \r\n                             | Reservation pod logs (first start) | `panic: no reachable servers` (timestamp 10:06:21) |                    \r\n                             | MongoDB‑reservation pod (`mongodb-reservation-5994859869-nsg4b`) | `phase=Running`, `ready=true`,            \r\n                             `startTime=2026‑10‑23T10:06:25Z` |                                                                             \r\n                             | Service `mongodb-reservation` endpoint | IP 10.244.162.189 (pod not ready until 10:06:25) |                  \r\n                             | No network policies or probes interfering – probes are `null` |                                              \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             **Fix**                                                                                                        \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             1. **Add a startup dependency** – make the reservation deployment wait for the MongoDB service to be ready,    \r\n                             e.g.:                                                                                                          \r\n                                - Use an **init container** that polls the MongoDB en"]
[505.764833, "o", "dpoint (`nc -z mongodb-reservation 27017`) before the  \r\n                             main container starts.                                                                                         \r\n                                - Or add a **readiness/liveness probe** that retries the DB connection and only marks the pod ready after a \r\n                             successful connection.                                                                                         \r\n                             2. **Improve connection handling** in the reservation code:                                                    \r\n                                - Implement retry logic with back‑off on initial DB connection failures.                                    \r\n                                - Exit with a non‑crash code (e.g., keep the process alive and retry) to avoid unnecessary restarts.        \r\n                             3. **Optional Helm ordering** – set `dependsOn` or `helm.sh/hook-weight` to ensure the MongoDB                 \r\n                             StatefulSet/Deployment is created and ready before the reservation deployment is rolled out.                   \r\n                                                                                                                                            \r\n                             Applying one of these changes will prevent the reservation pod from crashing on startup due to a transient “no \r\n                             reachable servers” error, eliminating the observed restarts.                                                   \r\n"]
