[701.664262, "o", "en the reservation pod started. Its `startTime` is                  \r\n           `2026‑10‑23T10:06:25Z`, while the reservation pod attempted the DB connection at `2026‑10‑23T10:06:21Z`. The DNS name            \r\n           resolved, but the service had no ready endpoints, causing the driver to report “no reachable servers”. The                       \r\n           reservation container crashed, was restarted (restartCount\\u202f=\\u202f2), and succeeded only after the DB became                \r\n           ready.  \\n\\n**Evidence**\\n\\n| Resource | Observation |\\n|----------|-------------|\\n| `reservation-57b8ccd5dc-48mqt`             \r\n           – container status | `lastState.terminated.exitCode=2`, `reason=Error`, `restartCount=2` |\\n| Reservation pod logs               \r\n           (first start) | `panic: no reachable servers` (timestamp\\u202f10:06:21) |\\n| MongoDB‑reservation pod                             \r\n           (`mongodb-reservation-5994859869-nsg4b`) | `phase=Running`, `ready=true`, `startTime=2026‑10‑23T10:06:25Z` |\\n|                  \r\n           Service `mongodb-reservation` endpoint | IP\\u202f10.244.162.189 (pod not ready until 10:06:25) |\\n| No network                   \r\n           policies or probes interfering – probes are `null` |\\n\\n**Fix**\\n\\n1. **Add a startup dependency** – make the                    \r\n           reservation deployment wait for the MongoDB service to be ready, e.g.:\\n   - Use an **init container** that polls the            \r\n           MongoDB endpoint (`nc -z mongodb-reservation 27017`) before the main container starts.\\n   - Or add a                            \r\n           **readiness/liveness probe** that retries the DB connection and only marks the pod ready after a successful                      \r\n           connection.\\n2. **Improve connection handling** in the reservation code:\\n   - Implement retry logic with back‑off on            \r\n           initial DB connection failures.\\n   - Exit with a non‑crash code (e.g., keep the process alive and retry) to avoid               \r\n           unnecessary restarts.\\n3. **Optional Helm ordering** – set `dependsOn` or `helm.sh/hook-weight` to ensure the MongoDB            \r\n           StatefulSet/Deployment is created and ready before the reservation deployment is rolled out.  \\n\\nApplying one of                \r\n           these changes will prevent the reservation pod from crashing on startup due to a transient “no reachable servers”                \r\n           error, eliminating the observed restarts.'}, 'TTL': 250.29841351509094, 'phase.fix_kubernetes.duration_s': 3.891,                \r\n           'phase.undeploy_leftovers.duration_s': 5.125, 'phase.deploy.duration_s': 259.265, 'phase.inject_fault.duration_s':               \r\n           7.137, 'phase.stage:diagnosis.duration_s': 216.673, 'phase.stage:diagnosis.outcome': 'submitted',                                \r\n           'phase.evaluate:diagnosis.duration_s': 33.396, 'phase.cleanup.duration_s': 162.073, 'run_status': 'complete'}                    \r\n"]
